# Print-in-place fit proofs for the three bodies (leaf A, leaf B, free pin).
# `fitcheck` renders every pairwise overlap and must be EMPTY (they clear —
# the pin is free, leaves don't rub). `fitcheck_neg` renders an oversized pin
# that MUST overlap the bores, proving the check can fail. This is the guard
# that catches the locked-hinge bug (a fused hinge scores 100/100 watertight;
# only this interference check sees it). `fold90` is the articulation proof:
# leaf B folded 90° must clear leaf A and the pin entirely — EMPTY means the
# hinge really swings (the check a teardrop pin fails; see NOTES.md).
fitcheck      empty
fitcheck_neg  interferes
fold90        empty
